	'k2d6d4c9d' => 'Wound dressing',
	'k2e058084' => 'Standard Visit Rates',
	'k2e3f10cd' => 'How We Work in Your Home',
	'k2f5ed502' => 'Physiotherapist Priya Raman joins a recovering patient for a 40-minute rehabilitation session. Beginning with gentle mobility exercises indoors, they step together onto the pavement outside for a steady walk down the quiet residential street. Priya monitors posture, pacing, and footing with a walking stick, helping the patient safely regain real-world balance, physical confidence, and personal mobility under gentle morning sunshine.',
	'k321cb271' => 'Nursing visit, 60 min',
	'k3281046b' => 'Three kinds of visit',
	'k3523ed5b' => 'Coordinated with your physician',
	'k355bb250' => 'The Haddad Family: Supported at Home',
	'k3603ace5' => 'Elise Moreau',
	'k36c07940' => 'Mr. Delacroix',
	'k36ef6391' => 'How a morning round<br>is walked',
	'k38d61860' => '03 Questions',
	'k39340111' => 'Sofia Brandt arrives for a specialized 60-minute wound and stoma visit. In a sunlit sitting room, she carefully removes the existing surgical dressing, inspects skin integrity, and cleanses the tissue using sterile technique. Sofia records healing progress in detail and applies fresh, comfortable dressings. Before departing, she reviews practical signs of infection with the patient and confirms necessary supplies for the week ahead.',
	'k395bd4e1' => 'Experiences in Care',
	'k3a677010' => 'Every 30 days',
	'k3ae3f4b3' => 'Cancellation',
	'k3c31060e' => 'Respect',
	'k3c8b020b' => 'Nursing that comes<br>to your living room.',
	'k3eb79eb9' => 'Story 01',
	'k3f38d1b3' => 'When home becomes<br>the ward',
	'k3f7052a2' => 'Rosa, 82, returned home after a hip operation, hesitant about walking alone.',
	'k420277c1' => 'Rehab walk on the street outside',
	'k443d6fc3' => 'At 82 years old, Rosa returned home to Linden Vale following a complex hip operation. Unfamiliar stairs and hallway thresholds felt daunting, and simple tasks like boiling a kettle required substantial effort. Our physiotherapist Priya Raman initiated a six-week programme of home rehabilitation visits. Early sessions focused on safe transfers between bed and chair, followed by balancing drills using the kitchen counter. Within three weeks, Rosa was practicing steady laps along her interior corridor with a walking frame. As strength improved, Priya accompanied Rosa outside onto the pavement. By the sixth week, Rosa felt confident navigating curbs and walking down the street to her neighborhood bakery with a single walking stick. Her experience illustrates how patient, home-based rehabilitation helps restore everyday mobility step by step.',
	'k44d626b1' => 'Cancellation Policy',
	'k457dd551' => 'Review',
	'k4587d7dd' => 'Review every 30 days',
	'k4667abc2' => 'Office Briefing',
	'k48becd09' => 'Signed by you, copy to your doctor',
	'k496eb563' => 'A thoughtful, written care plan ensures that your home visits are consistent, transparent, and closely aligned with your physician\'s guidance.',
